  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Jinka Area Maternal and Child Health Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Target groups:
Safe /Institutional delivery: 2,426 women
Contraceptive utilisation rate: 9,725 people
ANC first visit : 2,246 women
ANC fourth visit: 2,246 women
PNC: 2,426 women
PMTCT: 2,426 women 
Immunization Coverage: 2237 infants</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">eneralThis program is meant to improve health services for pregnant women, newborn babies and children in Jinka Area, South-Omo with an agro-pastoralists population. It aims at improved M&amp;CH practices at household and community level, increased reproductive health care attendance and improved capacity of health professionals, while working with the government for sustainability purposes.
This program is meant to improve health services for pregnant women, newborn babies and children in Jinka Area, South-Omo with an agro-pastoralists population. It aims at improved M&amp;CH practices at household and community level, increased reproductive health care attendance and improved capacity of health professionals, while working with the government for sustainability purposes.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022; Improved maternal and child health practices at household and community level &#x2022; Increased reproductive health care attendance (to increase reproductive health coverage). &#x2022; Improved Capacity of health professionals, CBOs and influential local parties. 
&#x2022; Improved maternal and child health practices at household and community level
